                <pb facs="0362" n="258" xml:id="pg258"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Abbott to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18, 1890</date>.
                        (Received August 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I acknowledge the receipt of your
                    instruction No. 67 of May 29 last, in which you direct me to maintain the
                    validity of the acts of Consul Vifquain in the matter of the Smith estate in
                    Colon.</p>
                <p>Dr. Roldàn informed me this morning, himself introducing the subject, that he
                    would discuss the matter with me as soon as possible, probably within 3 weeks,
                    and that he thought, we should have no difficulty in coming to an
                    understanding.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John T. Abbott.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
